ADR 001 choosing app code structure
status Accepted 
Date Oct. 5, 2026
Deciders Software dev team

What we are trying to solve
  We are designing an app that has calendar features, task scheduling, UI layout and cloud synching

What matters most
  easy to test: We want the testing to be easy so we don't have waste too much time checking features like sync
  easy to fix: When bugs apear we want to be able to fix get rid of them easily

Options we looked at
  MVC / MVVM Pattern (Layered Approach): Separates the app into three distinct parts: the screen layout (View), the background logic (Controller/ViewModel), and the saved data (Model).
  All-in-One Code (Monolith): Putting screen design, database connections, and sync logic all in the same files.

The decision
  We decided to use MVC/MVVM
  why?: we didn't want to go with all in one becasue we felt that mixing everything together could cause issues and make testing more difficult

The Good and Bad
  Good
    Independent Work: Designers can work on the screens while programmers work on background features like syncing.
    Simple Testing: We can run quick tests on the background logic without loading up the full UI.
  Bad
    Extra Setup: Requires a bit extra code and planning at the start instead of jumping straight into coding.  
